Where are we in the rework to remote the Python sim and replace it with the proper C++ bindings 
and behavioral, transactional, and temporal simulation models?

● Based on the status log and plans, here's the current state:

  Python → C++ Rework Status

  What's Working (v0.8.0+)
  ┌────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────┬───────────┐
  │      Mode      │              Compute              │                Memory                │  XUE Events  │  Status   │
  ├────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────┼───────────┤
  │ BEHAVIORAL     │ ✅ C++ BehavioralComputeFabric    │ ✅ C++ BehavioralMemoryController    │ ✅ Recording │ Fully C++ │
  ├────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────┼───────────┤
  │ TRANSACTIONAL  │ ✅ C++ TransactionalComputeFabric │ ✅ C++ TransactionalMemoryController │ ✅ Recording │ Fully C++ │
  ├────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────┼───────────┤
  │ CYCLE_ACCURATE │ ⚠️ Not exposed to Python          │ ⚠️ Not exposed to Python             │ N/A          │ C++ only  │
  └────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────┴───────────┘
  Operations in C++ Native Module

  ✅ Core ops:     matmul, linear, conv2d, conv3d
  ✅ Pooling:      maxpool2d, avgpool2d, adaptive_avgpool2d, maxpool3d, avgpool3d
  ✅ Norm:         batchnorm2d, batchnorm3d, layernorm
  ✅ Activation:   relu, gelu, silu, sigmoid, tanh, softmax
  ✅ Elementwise:  add, sub, mul, div (with TODO for broadcasting)
  ✅ Shape ops:    reshape, transpose, flatten, concat
  ✅ Reductions:   sum, mean, max, min
  ✅ Fused:        matmul_bias_relu, matmul_bias_gelu, conv2d_relu, conv2d_bn_relu
  ✅ Transformer:  attention (with QKV projections)

