❯ XUE Observation Architeture (OA) builds event hierarchies for resources that allow aggregation and drill down. For example, on a DRAM device, we
  measure low level cmds, so reads, writes, refreshes, etc. In the OA, we create new events by aggregating, so we would have TXN = reads + writes. We
  have event occurrences to count events, and we have occupancy and latency and time measured in clocks. With these we can then calculate X, U, and E.
  In our MLP example, we are not seeing these XUE event hierarchies, so this would not be sufficient for pre/post silicon validation. Please synthesize
  a comprehensive set of XUE OA event hierarchies, report these here for me to review.

● Let me design a comprehensive XUE Observation Architecture event hierarchy for MLP workloads. I'll present this for your review.

  ================================================================================
  XUE OBSERVATION ARCHITECTURE - MLP EVENT HIERARCHY SPECIFICATION
  ================================================================================

  The XUE OA provides hierarchical event aggregation enabling drill-down from
  high-level workload metrics to low-level resource operations. Each event
  tracks: count (occurrences), cycles (latency), and occupancy (busy/idle).

  From these primitives we derive:
    X = Throughput = work_done / cycles
    U = Utilization = busy_cycles / total_cycles
    E = Efficiency  = achieved / peak

  ================================================================================
  1. COMPUTE FABRIC EVENT HIERARCHY
  ================================================================================

                                MLP_INFERENCE
                                     │
                      ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
                      │              │              │
                 MLP_LAYER_0    MLP_LAYER_1    MLP_LAYER_N
                      │
          ┌───────────┼───────────┬───────────┐
          │           │           │           │
     MATMUL_OP   BIAS_ADD_OP  ACTIVATION  RESIDUAL_ADD
          │                       │
          │              ┌────────┼────────┐
          │              │        │        │
          │           RELU_OP  GELU_OP  SILU_OP
          │
     ┌────┴────┐
     │         │
  TILE_M×N  TILE_M×N  ... (tiled decomposition)
     │
     │ (16×16 systolic array operations)
     │
  ┌──┴──┬──────┬──────┬──────┐
  │     │      │      │      │
  MAC   MAC   MAC   MAC   ... (256 MACs/cycle for 16×16)


  COMPUTE EVENTS TABLE:
  ┌─────────────────────┬────────┬────────────┬────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Event               │ Level  │ Aggregates │ Metrics                        │
  ├─────────────────────┼────────┼────────────┼────────────────────────────────┤
  │ MAC                 │ L0     │ -          │ count, cycles=1                │
  │ TILE_16x16          │ L1     │ 256×MAC    │ count, cycles, flops=512       │
  │ MATMUL_TILE_MxN     │ L2     │ Σ TILE_16x16│ count, cycles, M, N, K        │
  │ MATMUL_OP           │ L3     │ Σ TILE_MxN │ count, cycles, total_flops     │
  │ ACTIVATION_ELEM     │ L0     │ -          │ count, cycles=1, type          │
  │ ACTIVATION_OP       │ L2     │ Σ ELEM     │ count, cycles, total_elems     │
  │ BIAS_ADD_OP         │ L2     │ -          │ count, cycles, elems           │
  │ MLP_LAYER           │ L4     │ MATMUL+ACT │ count, cycles, flops           │
  │ MLP_INFERENCE       │ L5     │ Σ LAYER    │ count, cycles, total_flops     │
  └─────────────────────┴────────┴────────────┴────────────────────────────────┘

  COMPUTE XUE METRICS:
    X_compute = total_flops / total_cycles                    [FLOPS/cycle]
    U_compute = systolic_busy_cycles / total_cycles           [0.0 - 1.0]
    E_compute = achieved_flops / (macs_per_cycle × 2 × U)     [0.0 - 1.0]

